          "hypothesis": "Cross-entropy on cosine similarities would produce a broadly useful robust encoder",
          "failure_mode": "Cosine similarity is invariant to radial rescaling: the loss can be minimized while arbitrarily distorting the unnormalized embedding, which LVLMs use directly. Mean clean embedding loss of 236.9 (TeCoA2) vs 0.0 (CLIP).",
          "lesson": "Need a loss that explicitly preserves the unnormalized embedding, not just its direction on the hypersphere. Led to the FARE embedding preservation objective.",
